$DIR/main.p:8:6: invalid use of C in the declaration of enum C
    An enum's member values cannot use the enum being declared, because those
    values are what decides the enum's integer type.
    (see "Enums" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.12)
    (run "pluto explain E2310" for a longer explanation)

